This data set comes with lots of columns! Let’s see how we would be able to narrow it down.

Select function






TipSyntax Alert





Functions in R are reusable blocks of code that accept inputs (arguments), perform operations (body) and return an output. 
Here is a function with a single argument, r

circumference &lt;- function(r) {
  # Function body: what the function does to input r
  2*pi*r
  # this function multiples 2 by pi by r to get the circumference
}

circumference(2)

[1] 12.56637


Here is a function with multiple arguments, x and y

subtract_two_nums &lt;- function(x, y){
  # Function body: what the function does to inputs x and y
  x - y
  # this function subtracts y from x
}

subtract_two_nums(3, 1)

[1] 2





We can use the select() function to create a new data set that only has the desired columns. Test it out below! Pay attention to how the column names inside the select() functions changes as you change what columns to include.

